       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as ORD-0001: amlodipine 50 mg by mouth, once daily.\n\nI added a note to the order saying the dose is above the usual maximum. The note says it's intentional, was recommended by the specialist after standard dosing failed, and is documented in the chart. It also asks for pharmacy verification and close monitoring.\n\nBecause of the dose, I'd suggest:\n- Frequent BP and heart rate checks, especially in the first several doses.\n- Hold parameters for hypotension or symptomatic bradycardia or tachycardia.\n- Watching for peripheral edema and dizziness or falls risk.\n- Pharmacy review, since they may call to verify the dose."
